(4. Component Specifications) Tj
0 -24 Td
/F1 14 Tf
(4.1 Ingestion Layer) Tj
0 -20 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(The ingestion layer receives events from three source systems: CRM, ERP,) Tj
0 -16 Td
(and IoT sensor network. Events are validated against Avro schemas stored) Tj
0 -16 Td
(in the Schema Registry before being forwarded downstream.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(Throughput target: 500,000 events per second at p99 < 50ms latency.) Tj
0 -24 Td
/F1 14 Tf
(4.2 Storage Layer) Tj
0 -20 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(Raw events are written to Bronze Delta tables. The daily compaction job) Tj
0 -16 Td
(merges Bronze into Silver (cleaned) and Silver into Gold (aggregated).) Tj
0 -16 Td
(Retention policy: Bronze 7 days, Silver 90 days, Gold unlimited.) Tj
0 -24 Td
/F1 14 Tf
(4.3 Query Layer) Tj
0 -20 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(Trino is deployed as a 24-node cluster: 4 coordinators and 20 workers.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(Adaptive query execution is enabled. Result caching uses Alluxio.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(SLA: 95th percentile query latency < 2 seconds for dashboard queries.) Tj
0 -24 Td
/F1 14 Tf
(5. Security) Tj
0 -20 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(All inter-service communication uses mTLS. API authentication uses JWTs) Tj
0 -16 Td
(issued by the internal identity provider (Keycloak). Data at rest is) Tj
0 -16 Td
(encrypted with AWS KMS. David Park owns the threat model review cycle.) Tj
ET
